      "content": "The core of the conflict is the competing national claims of the Jewish and Arab peoples to the same piece of land, the historical land of the Levant.  Zionism, the political movement for a Jewish national home in the area, gained strength in the 19th and 20th centuries, often in response to anti-semitism in Europe. This growing political and religious desire for a national state, combined with the strong nationalist feelings of the local, predominantly Arab population, set the stage for the intense political and ideological struggle that defines the conflict.",
