      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The main motivation for the strong rejection was the belief that the partition was fundamentally illegitimate, as it carved up the land to favor the in-migrating, politically powerful Zionist entity in a way that deeply disrespected the established rights and political power of the local, overwhelmingly Arab population. For the Arab side, the plan represented a targeted political division that went against the self-determination principles they felt should apply to the majority community on the ground.\n\nThe Jewish side, on the other hand, viewed the UN vote as a legitimate political endorsement of the right to self-determination for the Jewish people in their historical and religious homeland, and saw the partition as the essential first step towards statehood after 2,000 years of unaddressed political needs and systemic discrimination in the surrounding mandatory power structure.",
